{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T12:24:48.962Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"45","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (64e62e2c). CONFIRMED AS A DEFECT, REFUTED AS STATED. The reviewer's premise — that cognee, graphiti, letta and supermemory 'also rely on in-process _buffers and raise BUFFER_MISSING' — is false for this kit: 'grep -rn BUFFER_MISSING bench/memory' hits only entire, cmm, bm25 and graphify. Those four arms have NO ADAPTER AT ALL, so a run dies at client construction, before ingestion ever starts. Adding them to the buffer list would have printed a FALSE REASON while leaving the real hole open — 'run_locomo.sh cognee' without resume would still have been accepted.\n\nFixed the actual defect class instead: the launcher now validates against the FACTORY's own sets (BUNDLED_ARMS / UNVENDORED_ARMS with an adapter-existence gate, exit 5), and resume refusal additionally extends to any SUPPLIED adapter carrying the BUFFER_MISSING guard — so launcher and factory cannot drift apart. Fail-without-fix: 'test_an_unvendored_arm_is_refused_with_the_factorys_reason: 5 != 1', where rc 1 means the run reached exec, i.e. was accepted. Python suite 47 tests OK, up from 40.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NPR3SPQC0X41W9ZZ8KN5G9","targetId":"01M1NPR3SX2M0MVXCKPSR91NMC","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NFS376AAYQ3JWAE76AZH3T"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
