{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:21:40.935Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"12","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (25e6d102). CONFIRMED behaviourally: a fake stock binary via CMM_BIN was accepted and would have scored as the patched row ('RuntimeError not raised'). Fix requires positive identification and never falls back. CMM_BIN is now REQUIRED with no PATH default — a bare name is still allowed but must be NAMED, not discovered — plus CMM_BUILD = patched (default) | stock. The resolved binary is fingerprinted WITHOUT executing it: patch 0005's two BM25 exclusion lists are adjacent C string literals, so each form survives compilation verbatim in .rodata and the file is byte-scanned in 1 MiB chunks with an overlap window (a chunk-boundary test pins that). A stock binary under a 'patched' declaration raises CMM_UNPATCHED_BINARY naming the published row and the patch; patched-under-stock and neither-fingerprint (CMM_UNVERIFIED_BINARY) also abort, with no fallback in any cell. Notably test_the_build_fingerprints_are_the_patch_0005_exclusion_lists ties the fingerprints to the PATCH TEXT rather than to a copy of themselves, so the check cannot rot into a tautology. README section 2 step 6, 3.3 (3x2 build/declaration table) and 4 updated to match; the sibling home-directory-default guard stays green.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NFVHVHKZ8W06722NDQXCFQ","targetId":"01M1NFVHVRYPBVD75XGNC5A5PT","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NFS376AAYQ3JWAE76AZH3T"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
