{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:51:53.707Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"25","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (5afb86d1). CONFIRMED, and it is a VERIFICATION BYPASS rather than a cosmetic path issue. Repro: a patched fake binary in cwd with CMM_BIN=./codebase-memory-mcp and PATH=/nonexistent gave client.binary == 'codebase-memory-mcp', isabs False, shutil.which None — so the patched-build fingerprint was computed against the LOCAL file while subprocess would have resolved a bare name on PATH. Verification and execution could target different binaries, defeating the check entirely. './name' is now preserved as the deliberate 'in this directory' spelling it is. Fail-without-fix: 'the run would execute .../elsewhere/codebase-memory-mcp, which is not the binary that was verified at construction'. The stock-binary refusal is unweakened — a relative SHIPPED binary is still refused, pinned by its own test.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NHFMPGKKRCEARXNYG0DP50","targetId":"01M1NHFMPN66PYGXCX05TQBNZ7","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NFS376AAYQ3JWAE76AZH3T"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
